by adrianrudnik at 2026-06-16T16:46:43Z

Sure, thanks for the review! I also looked into frankenphp and how it would be solved over there. Just to document it here, it would require a specific [set of configuration](https://frankenphp.dev/docs/config/#watching-for-file-changes), as `css` files are not within the default file mask of `./**/*.{env,php,twig,yaml,yml}` that is watched:

```caddy
	frankenphp {
		worker {
			file ./public/index.php
			watch var/tailwind/**/*.css
		}
	}
```

then run it with `--watch`, this also solves it by forcing a worker restart on detected changes.
